{
  "rules": [
    "Regime shift / trend underreaction: when spot breaks out upward (new 30d highs), the model systematically underestimates the subsequent 2–4 week path. Apply a positive drift adjustment that grows with horizon (small in days 1–5, larger in days 15–30).",
    "Late-horizon upside miss: forecasts beyond ~day 20 are biased low during rallies; add an increasing uplift toward the end of the forecast window, especially if the last 5–10 historical closes are rising.",
    "Over-mean-reversion after strength: following strong up-moves, the model pulls back toward mid/high-60s too quickly; dampen mean-reversion strength when momentum is positive (e.g., keep forecasts closer to recent highs).",
    "Volatility compression: the model’s forecast range is too narrow; increase variance/allow higher highs and lower lows, with emphasis on permitting upside extension in bullish regimes.",
    "Turning-point lag: the model is slow to recognize accelerations (and likely decelerations); incorporate a momentum trigger (e.g., slope of last 5–10 days) to shift the whole forecast path up/down earlier rather than gradually."
  ]
}
